-## 5. Changing it
+## 5. While the game runs (first visits)
+
+What the cache cannot know ahead (vertex shader variants per vertex layout, pipelines of new state combinations) is
+compiled when first drawn. Those draws wait within a per-frame budget (`native_x_renderer_scene_wait_ms`, D116; a
+game exposes it as a setting, Mad Riders' F1 > New shaders, 8 ms by default) and are skipped past it; a frame with 8 or
+more skipped draws lets the next one wait up to 33 ms (a burst: a race's start, D117). Pipelines compile on cores − 2
+threads (4–12), translations on 2 workers, every core but one during a burst of more than 4.
+
+## 6. Changing it
 
 - A new kind of record: add a `Kind`, write it with `AddLocked` (journaled) or like `SetDriverCache` (only with the
   whole file), read it in `Open`'s final loop.
